- Write no `claims`. Every location whose relation counts carries `clauses`; a strong relation names them all and carries `instantiation` and `tests`, as does a `hasPart` whose `conjunct_relation` is strong; a `relatedMatch` names none. A `hasPart` or `narrowMatch` carries `step`, and only those two do; a `hasPart` of a compound statement carries `conjunct_relation`, and only it does; a `closeMatch` carries `convention`, and only a `closeMatch` does. `instantiation`, `step` and each test are one line each, of at least three words of your own: "n/a" is no answer.
- `located`: at least one location whose relation is not `relatedMatch`; at most {{max_locations}}, ranked 1.. without repeats, best first. `confidence` is one of `high`, `medium`, `low`.
- `absent`: you searched and nothing in the universe states it, or any clause of it. The receipt lists **at least {{min_absence_queries}} distinct queries** (and at least one per clause) and the candidates you examined, and its `query_clauses` tags every query with the clauses it targets. It names in `special_case` the nearest special-case candidate you found and why it is not one, or says why none exists. An absence may sit beside `relatedMatch` locations only, never while a curated candidate is left unexamined, and never with a candidate rejected for stating part of the passage.
- `unresolved`: you could not decide, or the cut is wrong — the passage states nothing a library could state, or it holds several statements the inventory did not cut. That is the inventory's defect, which you cannot re-cut: say so with a `cut_flag`, one of {{cut_flags}}, and name the statements in `reason`. It is counted as unresolved, never as not formalized — prefer it to a guess.
- `coverage` (a `located` compound statement only): `parts` are the `rank`s of at least {{min_coverage_parts}} of this passage's `hasPart` locations, whose `clauses` partition the conjuncts and whose `conjunct_relation`s are strong, and `note` says in one sentence of your own how they together state every conjunct. Never on a simple statement, or on an `absent` or `unresolved` passage.
- Copy `item`, the source's shas and `renderer` from the manifest exactly; write no commit and no `proof_status`.
- Write each `note`, query, `reason`, test and line **in your own words**: one that copies more than {{quote_max_words}} consecutive words of the article is refused, since the published records quote no more than that.

